WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.520
Welcome to Process Quality Assurance. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Evaluate process use objectively and resolve process noncompliance.

2
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:20.450
Consider this scenario. Procedures are published but no one checks actual use. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:30.810
Start with two steps: Define objective evaluation criteria. Then Examine actual practice. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:39.640
Continue with Communicate findings. Then Track corrective resolution. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:39.640 --> 00:01:00.190
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous evaluation criteria, noncompliance log, closure evidence tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: letting the same team be its only independent assurance; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:14.440
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
